# Per-Dockerfile ignore file — governs every build of `Dockerfile` (BuildKit
# prefers `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over the context root's shared
# `.dockerignore` and does NOT read the shared one when this file exists). The
# old packaging layer used the same per-Dockerfile binding (a file named after
# its Dockerfile), so this repo keeps that convention rather than the generic
# `.dockerignore` name.
#
# Everything below is excluded from the context upload. The Dockerfile COPYs
# exactly these paths — pyproject.toml, uv.lock, README.md, LICENSE and src/ —
# so NONE of them may appear in this list. (The predecessor file excluded a
# root-level README.md and LICENSE; that was the other repo's copy. Here those
# names are this image's build inputs, so the exclusions were dropped, not
# ported.)

# VCS
.git
**/.git

# Python scratch a local checkout carries — never build inputs.
.venv
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.mypy_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Local runtime config — untracked, may hold a real secret. The demo stack
# bind-mounts the generated config at /app/config.json instead.
config.json

# Secrets and live state — must never be baked into any image.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Repo files that are not inputs to this build (root-level matches only).
# README.md and LICENSE deliberately do NOT appear here — the Dockerfile COPYs
# them.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.dockerignore
.github
.gitignore
.python-version
AGENTS.md
REFERENCE.md
config.example.json
scripts
